<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Appendix of Theoretical Analysis</h2>

<section id="A1.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.1 </span>Full version of Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma1" title="Lemma 1 (Implicit Weight). ‣ 5.2 Stability of Prompt Updates ‣ 5 Theoretical Analysis ‣ Graph-based Target Back-Propagation for Context Adaptation in Multi-LLM Agentic Systems" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a></h3>

<div id="Thmlemmafullx1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemmafull">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmlemmafullx1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma </span><a href="#Thmlemma1" title="Lemma 1 (Implicit Weight). ‣ 5.2 Stability of Prompt Updates ‣ 5 Theoretical Analysis ‣ Graph-based Target Back-Propagation for Context Adaptation in Multi-LLM Agentic Systems" class="ltx_ref ltx_font_bold"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a></span><span id="Thmlemmafullx1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmlemmafullx1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmlemmafullx1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemmafullx1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For a transformer block with frozen parameters, let <math id="Thmlemmafullx1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> denote the update
iteration of GTBP. Changing the prompt from <math id="Thmlemmafullx1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{v}^{(t-1)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>v</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{v}^{(t-1)}</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="Thmlemmafullx1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{v}^{(t)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>v</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{v}^{(t)}</annotation></semantics></math>
can be interpreted as inducing an effective inference-time weight update
<math id="Thmlemmafullx1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta W_{v}^{(t)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>v</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta W_{v}^{(t)}</annotation></semantics></math>, i.e.,</span></p>
<table id="A1.E10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{W_{v}}\!\left(\pi_{v}^{(t)},x_{v}\right)=T_{W_{v}+\Delta W_{v}^{(t)}}\!\left(\pi_{v}^{(t-1)},x_{v}\right)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>v</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>v</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>v</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>v</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{W_{v}}\!\left(\pi_{v}^{(t)},x_{v}\right)=T_{W_{v}+\Delta W_{v}^{(t)}}\!\left(\pi_{v}^{(t-1)},x_{v}\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(10)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmlemmafullx1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemmafullx1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where</span></p>
<table id="A1.E11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta W_{v}^{(t)}=\frac{\left(W_{v}\,\delta A_{v}\!\left(\pi_{v}^{(t)},\pi_{v}^{(t-1)}\right)\right)A_{v}(\pi_{v}^{(t-1)})^{\top}}{\|A_{v}(\pi_{v}^{(t-1)})\|_{2}^{2}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>v</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>v</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>v</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>v</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>v</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta W_{v}^{(t)}=\frac{\left(W_{v}\,\delta A_{v}\!\left(\pi_{v}^{(t)},\pi_{v}^{(t-1)}\right)\right)A_{v}(\pi_{v}^{(t-1)})^{\top}}{\|A_{v}(\pi_{v}^{(t-1)})\|_{2}^{2}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(11)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmlemmafullx1.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemmafullx1.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">with</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta A_{v}\!\left(\pi_{v}^{(t)},\pi_{v}^{(t-1)}\right):=A_{v}\!\left(\pi_{v}^{(t)}\right)-A_{v}\!\left(\pi_{v}^{(t-1)}\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>v</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>v</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>v</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>v</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta A_{v}\!\left(\pi_{v}^{(t)},\pi_{v}^{(t-1)}\right):=A_{v}\!\left(\pi_{v}^{(t)}\right)-A_{v}\!\left(\pi_{v}^{(t-1)}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.2 </span>Proof of Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 1. ‣ 5.2 Stability of Prompt Updates ‣ 5 Theoretical Analysis ‣ Graph-based Target Back-Propagation for Context Adaptation in Multi-LLM Agentic Systems" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a></h3>

<div id="A1.SS2.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A1.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">Taking the Frobenius norm on both sides of Eq. <a href="#A1.E11" title="In Lemma . ‣ A.1 Full version of Lemma ‣ Appendix A Appendix of Theoretical Analysis ‣ Graph-based Target Back-Propagation for Context Adaptation in Multi-LLM Agentic Systems" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">11</span></a> and using
<math id="A1.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|uv^{\top}\|_{F}=\|u\|_{2}\|v\|_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|uv^{\top}\|_{F}=\|u\|_{2}\|v\|_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, we obtain</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx1" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex10"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\|\Delta W_{v}^{(t)}\|_{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>v</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\|\Delta W_{v}^{(t)}\|_{F}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex11"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{\left\|W_{v}\bigl(A_{v}(\pi_{v}^{(t)},x_{v})-A_{v}(\pi_{v}^{(t-1)},x_{v})\bigr)\right\|_{2}}{\|A_{v}(\pi_{v}^{(t-1)},x_{v})\|_{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>v</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>v</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>v</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{\left\|W_{v}\bigl(A_{v}(\pi_{v}^{(t)},x_{v})-A_{v}(\pi_{v}^{(t-1)},x_{v})\bigr)\right\|_{2}}{\|A_{v}(\pi_{v}^{(t-1)},x_{v})\|_{2}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex12"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\frac{\|W_{v}\|_{2}\|A_{v}(\pi_{v}^{(t)},x_{v})-A_{v}(\pi_{v}^{(t-1)},x_{v})\|_{2}}{\|A_{v}(\pi_{v}^{(t-1)},x_{v})\|_{2}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>v</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>v</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>v</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\frac{\|W_{v}\|_{2}\|A_{v}(\pi_{v}^{(t)},x_{v})-A_{v}(\pi_{v}^{(t-1)},x_{v})\|_{2}}{\|A_{v}(\pi_{v}^{(t-1)},x_{v})\|_{2}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text">By Assumption <a href="#Thmassumption1" title="Assumption 1 (Prompt-length stability). ‣ 5.2 Stability of Prompt Updates ‣ 5 Theoretical Analysis ‣ Graph-based Target Back-Propagation for Context Adaptation in Multi-LLM Agentic Systems" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>,</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex13" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|A_{v}(\pi_{v}^{(t)},x_{v})-A_{v}(\pi_{v}^{(t-1)},x_{v})\|_{2}=\mathcal{O}(t^{-1})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>v</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>v</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|A_{v}(\pi_{v}^{(t)},x_{v})-A_{v}(\pi_{v}^{(t-1)},x_{v})\|_{2}=\mathcal{O}(t^{-1}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text">By Assumption <a href="#Thmassumption2" title="Assumption 2. ‣ 5.2 Stability of Prompt Updates ‣ 5 Theoretical Analysis ‣ Graph-based Target Back-Propagation for Context Adaptation in Multi-LLM Agentic Systems" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>,</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex14" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|A_{v}(\pi_{v}^{(t-1)},x_{v})\|_{2}\geq\gamma_{v}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>v</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>v</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|A_{v}(\pi_{v}^{(t-1)},x_{v})\|_{2}\geq\gamma_{v}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p1.4.1" class="ltx_text">Therefore,</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex15" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\Delta W_{v}^{(t)}\|_{F}\leq\frac{\|W_{v}\|_{2}}{\gamma_{v}}\mathcal{O}(t^{-1})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>v</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mfrac><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>v</mi></msub></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\Delta W_{v}^{(t)}\|_{F}\leq\frac{\|W_{v}\|_{2}}{\gamma_{v}}\mathcal{O}(t^{-1}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p1.5.1" class="ltx_text">Since <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{v}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{v}</annotation></semantics></math> is frozen, <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|W_{v}\|_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|W_{v}\|_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> is a constant. Hence,</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex16" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\Delta W_{v}^{(t)}\|_{F}=\mathcal{O}(t^{-1})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>v</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\Delta W_{v}^{(t)}\|_{F}=\mathcal{O}(t^{-1}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p1.6.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.3 </span>Proof of Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem 2. ‣ 5.2 Stability of Prompt Updates ‣ 5 Theoretical Analysis ‣ Graph-based Target Back-Propagation for Context Adaptation in Multi-LLM Agentic Systems" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a></h3>

<div id="A1.SS3.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A1.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">By Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma1" title="Lemma 1 (Implicit Weight). ‣ 5.2 Stability of Prompt Updates ‣ 5 Theoretical Analysis ‣ Graph-based Target Back-Propagation for Context Adaptation in Multi-LLM Agentic Systems" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>, the prompt update from
<math id="A1.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{v}^{(t-1)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>v</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{v}^{(t-1)}</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{v}^{(t)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>v</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{v}^{(t)}</annotation></semantics></math> can be represented as an
input-dependent effective weight update <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta W_{v,I_{v}}^{(t)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>v</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta W_{v,I_{v}}^{(t)}</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus,
for the local target loss, we can write</span></p>
<table id="A1.SS3.p1.2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.SS3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell\!\left(M_{v}(I_{v};\pi_{v}^{(t)}),\hat{O}_{v}\right)\\
=\ell\!\left(M_{v,W_{v}+\Delta W_{v,I_{v}}^{(t)}}(I_{v};\pi_{v}^{(t-1)}),\hat{O}_{v}\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.077em;" width="0.077em"><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>v</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>O</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>v</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.077em;" width="0.077em"><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>v</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>v</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>O</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>v</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell\!\left(M_{v}(I_{v};\pi_{v}^{(t)}),\hat{O}_{v}\right)\\
=\ell\!\left(M_{v,W_{v}+\Delta W_{v,I_{v}}^{(t)}}(I_{v};\pi_{v}^{(t-1)}),\hat{O}_{v}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS3.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text">Define the per-sample local target loss as</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex17" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{v,t-1}(W_{v}):=\ell\!\left(M_{v}(I_{v};\pi_{v}^{(t-1)}),\hat{O}_{v}\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.247em;" width="0.247em"><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>v</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>O</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>v</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{v,t-1}(W_{v}):=\ell\!\left(M_{v}(I_{v};\pi_{v}^{(t-1)}),\hat{O}_{v}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.p1.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS3.p1.4.1" class="ltx_text">Then, using <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝔼</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}</annotation></semantics></math> as shorthand for <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{(x,y^{*})\sim\mathcal{T}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{(x,y^{*})\sim\mathcal{T}}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</span></p>
<table id="A1.E12" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{v}(\pi_{v}^{(t)})-F_{v}(\pi_{v}^{(t-1)})\\
=\mathbb{E}\left[f_{v,t-1}(W_{v}+\Delta W_{v,I_{v}}^{(t)})-f_{v,t-1}(W_{v})\right]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>v</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>v</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>v</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{v}(\pi_{v}^{(t)})-F_{v}(\pi_{v}^{(t-1)})\\
=\mathbb{E}\left[f_{v,t-1}(W_{v}+\Delta W_{v,I_{v}}^{(t)})-f_{v,t-1}(W_{v})\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(12)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">By Assumption <a href="#Thmassumption3" title="Assumption 3 (Per-sample regularity). ‣ 5.2 Stability of Prompt Updates ‣ 5 Theoretical Analysis ‣ Graph-based Target Back-Propagation for Context Adaptation in Multi-LLM Agentic Systems" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>, <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{v,t-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{v,t-1}</annotation></semantics></math> is second-order
smooth along the segment from <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{v}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{v}</annotation></semantics></math> to
<math id="A1.SS3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{v}+\Delta W_{v,I_{v}}^{(t)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>v</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{v}+\Delta W_{v,I_{v}}^{(t)}</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore,</span></p>
<table id="A1.E13" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left|f_{v,t-1}(W_{v}+\Delta W_{v,I_{v}}^{(t)})-f_{v,t-1}(W_{v})\right|\\
\leq\left|\left\langle\nabla f_{v,t-1}(W_{v}),\Delta W_{v,I_{v}}^{(t)}\right\rangle\right|+\frac{L_{v}}{2}\left\|\Delta W_{v,I_{v}}^{(t)}\right\|_{F}^{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>v</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>v</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>v</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left|f_{v,t-1}(W_{v}+\Delta W_{v,I_{v}}^{(t)})-f_{v,t-1}(W_{v})\right|\\
\leq\left|\left\langle\nabla f_{v,t-1}(W_{v}),\Delta W_{v,I_{v}}^{(t)}\right\rangle\right|+\frac{L_{v}}{2}\left\|\Delta W_{v,I_{v}}^{(t)}\right\|_{F}^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(13)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS3.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">By the bounded-gradient condition in
Assumption <a href="#Thmassumption3" title="Assumption 3 (Per-sample regularity). ‣ 5.2 Stability of Prompt Updates ‣ 5 Theoretical Analysis ‣ Graph-based Target Back-Propagation for Context Adaptation in Multi-LLM Agentic Systems" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>, we assume that there exists
<math id="A1.SS3.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{v}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{v}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> such that</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex18" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left\|\nabla f_{v,t-1}(W_{v})\right\|_{F}\leq G_{v}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>v</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\|\nabla f_{v,t-1}(W_{v})\right\|_{F}\leq G_{v}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.p2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS3.p2.3.1" class="ltx_text">Then, by Cauchy–Schwarz, the first term on the right-hand side of
Eq. <a href="#A1.E13" title="In Proof. ‣ A.3 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix A Appendix of Theoretical Analysis ‣ Graph-based Target Back-Propagation for Context Adaptation in Multi-LLM Agentic Systems" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">13</span></a> satisfies</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx2" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex19"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left|\left\langle\nabla f_{v,t-1}(W_{v}),\Delta W_{v,I_{v}}^{(t)}\right\rangle\right|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>v</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left|\left\langle\nabla f_{v,t-1}(W_{v}),\Delta W_{v,I_{v}}^{(t)}\right\rangle\right|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex20"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\|\nabla f_{v,t-1}(W_{v})\|_{F}\left\|\Delta W_{v,I_{v}}^{(t)}\right\|_{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>v</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\|\nabla f_{v,t-1}(W_{v})\|_{F}\left\|\Delta W_{v,I_{v}}^{(t)}\right\|_{F}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex21"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq G_{v}\left\|\Delta W_{v,I_{v}}^{(t)}\right\|_{F}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>v</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq G_{v}\left\|\Delta W_{v,I_{v}}^{(t)}\right\|_{F}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.p2.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS3.p2.4.1" class="ltx_text">Hence, we can rewrite Eq. <a href="#A1.E13" title="In Proof. ‣ A.3 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix A Appendix of Theoretical Analysis ‣ Graph-based Target Back-Propagation for Context Adaptation in Multi-LLM Agentic Systems" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">13</span></a> as</span></p>
<table id="A1.E14" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left|f_{v,t-1}(W_{v}+\Delta W_{v,I_{v}}^{(t)})-f_{v,t-1}(W_{v})\right|\\
\leq G_{v}\left\|\Delta W_{v,I_{v}}^{(t)}\right\|_{F}+\frac{L_{v}}{2}\left\|\Delta W_{v,I_{v}}^{(t)}\right\|_{F}^{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>v</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>v</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>v</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left|f_{v,t-1}(W_{v}+\Delta W_{v,I_{v}}^{(t)})-f_{v,t-1}(W_{v})\right|\\
\leq G_{v}\left\|\Delta W_{v,I_{v}}^{(t)}\right\|_{F}+\frac{L_{v}}{2}\left\|\Delta W_{v,I_{v}}^{(t)}\right\|_{F}^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(14)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS3.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">By Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 1. ‣ 5.2 Stability of Prompt Updates ‣ 5 Theoretical Analysis ‣ Graph-based Target Back-Propagation for Context Adaptation in Multi-LLM Agentic Systems" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>, we have that</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex22" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left\|\Delta W_{v,I_{v}}^{(t)}\right\|_{F}=\mathcal{O}(t^{-1})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>v</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\|\Delta W_{v,I_{v}}^{(t)}\right\|_{F}=\mathcal{O}(t^{-1}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS3.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">which leads to</span></p>
<table id="A1.E15" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}\left[\left\|\Delta W_{v,I_{v}}^{(t)}\right\|_{F}\right]=\mathcal{O}(t^{-1})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>v</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}\left[\left\|\Delta W_{v,I_{v}}^{(t)}\right\|_{F}\right]=\mathcal{O}(t^{-1}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(15)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.p3.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS3.p3.3.1" class="ltx_text">and</span></p>
<table id="A1.E16" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}\left[\left\|\Delta W_{v,I_{v}}^{(t)}\right\|_{F}^{2}\right]=\mathcal{O}(t^{-2})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>v</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}\left[\left\|\Delta W_{v,I_{v}}^{(t)}\right\|_{F}^{2}\right]=\mathcal{O}(t^{-2}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(16)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.p3.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS3.p3.4.1" class="ltx_text">Therefore, by combining Eqs. <a href="#A1.E12" title="In Proof. ‣ A.3 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix A Appendix of Theoretical Analysis ‣ Graph-based Target Back-Propagation for Context Adaptation in Multi-LLM Agentic Systems" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">12</span></a>, <a href="#A1.E14" title="In Proof. ‣ A.3 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix A Appendix of Theoretical Analysis ‣ Graph-based Target Back-Propagation for Context Adaptation in Multi-LLM Agentic Systems" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">14</span></a>, <a href="#A1.E15" title="In Proof. ‣ A.3 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix A Appendix of Theoretical Analysis ‣ Graph-based Target Back-Propagation for Context Adaptation in Multi-LLM Agentic Systems" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">15</span></a>, and <a href="#A1.E16" title="In Proof. ‣ A.3 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix A Appendix of Theoretical Analysis ‣ Graph-based Target Back-Propagation for Context Adaptation in Multi-LLM Agentic Systems" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">16</span></a>, we obtain</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx3" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex23"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left|F_{v}(\pi_{v}^{(t)})-F_{v}(\pi_{v}^{(t-1)})\right|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>v</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>v</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left|F_{v}(\pi_{v}^{(t)})-F_{v}(\pi_{v}^{(t-1)})\right|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex24"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\mathbb{E}\left[\left|f_{v,t-1}(W_{v}+\Delta W_{v,I_{v}}^{(t)})-f_{v,t-1}(W_{v})\right|\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>v</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\mathbb{E}\left[\left|f_{v,t-1}(W_{v}+\Delta W_{v,I_{v}}^{(t)})-f_{v,t-1}(W_{v})\right|\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex25"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathcal{O}(t^{-1})+\mathcal{O}(t^{-2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathcal{O}(t^{-1})+\mathcal{O}(t^{-2})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex26"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathcal{O}(t^{-1})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathcal{O}(t^{-1}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS3.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.4 </span>Proof of Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem3" title="Theorem 3. ‣ 5.3 Gradient-Aligned Implicit Updates ‣ 5 Theoretical Analysis ‣ Graph-based Target Back-Propagation for Context Adaptation in Multi-LLM Agentic Systems" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a></h3>

<div id="A1.SS4.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A1.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex27" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F(\Pi_{\Phi})=\mathbb{E}_{(x,y^{*})\sim\mathcal{T}}\left[\ell\!\left(\Phi(x;\Pi_{\Phi}),y^{*}\right)\right]" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.247em;" width="0.247em"><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F(\Pi_{\Phi})=\mathbb{E}_{(x,y^{*})\sim\mathcal{T}}\left[\ell\!\left(\Phi(x;\Pi_{\Phi}),y^{*}\right)\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS4.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS4.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text">denote the overall objective in Eq. <a href="#S3.E4" title="In 3 Problem Formulation ‣ Graph-based Target Back-Propagation for Context Adaptation in Multi-LLM Agentic Systems" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>. For the
one-hidden-layer workflow, the intermediate responses at iteration <math id="A1.SS4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> are</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex28" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex28.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="O_{k}^{(t)}=M_{k}(x;\pi_{k}^{(t)}),\qquad k=1,\dots,K," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>O</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>;</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O_{k}^{(t)}=M_{k}(x;\pi_{k}^{(t)}),\qquad k=1,\dots,K,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS4.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS4.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text">and the final output is</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex29" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y^{(t)}=M_{\mathrm{out}}\left(x,O_{1}^{(t)},\dots,O_{K}^{(t)};\pi_{\mathrm{out}}^{(t)}\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>y</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>out</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>O</mi><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>O</mi><mi>K</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>out</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y^{(t)}=M_{\mathrm{out}}\left(x,O_{1}^{(t)},\dots,O_{K}^{(t)};\pi_{\mathrm{out}}^{(t)}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS4.p1.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS4.p1.4.1" class="ltx_text">Consider the prompt-update step for the first-layer modules. Sufficiently small
<math id="A1.SS4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon_{\mathrm{opt},k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mrow><mi>opt</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon_{\mathrm{opt},k}</annotation></semantics></math> means that the LLM optimizer is powerful enough
to generate prompts whose outputs are close to the inferred local targets. Thus, for each first-layer node <math id="A1.SS4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>, the updated response becomes
sufficiently close to its inferred local target <math id="A1.SS4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{O}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>O</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{O}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Since <math id="A1.SS4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> is finite, the aggregated input received by the output node</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex30" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I_{\mathrm{out}}^{(t)}=(x,O_{1}^{(t)},\dots,O_{K}^{(t)})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>I</mi><mi>out</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>O</mi><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>O</mi><mi>K</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I_{\mathrm{out}}^{(t)}=(x,O_{1}^{(t)},\dots,O_{K}^{(t)})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS4.p1.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS4.p1.5.1" class="ltx_text">also
close to the target-consistent input</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex31" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex31.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{I}_{\mathrm{out}}=(x,\hat{O}_{1},\dots,\hat{O}_{K})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>I</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>out</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>O</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>O</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>K</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{I}_{\mathrm{out}}=(x,\hat{O}_{1},\dots,\hat{O}_{K}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS4.p1.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS4.p1.6.1" class="ltx_text">By Assumption <a href="#Thmassumption1" title="Assumption 1 (Prompt-length stability). ‣ 5.2 Stability of Prompt Updates ‣ 5 Theoretical Analysis ‣ Graph-based Target Back-Propagation for Context Adaptation in Multi-LLM Agentic Systems" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> applied to the output node,
the contextual representation change induced by the updated output-node input
and prompt is <math id="A1.SS4.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(t^{-1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(t^{-1})</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore, by
Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem 2. ‣ 5.2 Stability of Prompt Updates ‣ 5 Theoretical Analysis ‣ Graph-based Target Back-Propagation for Context Adaptation in Multi-LLM Agentic Systems" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>, the corresponding change in the
output-node local target objective is also <math id="A1.SS4.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(t^{-1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(t^{-1})</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<table id="A1.E17" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left|F_{\mathrm{out}}(I_{\mathrm{out}}^{(t)},\pi_{\mathrm{out}}^{(t)})-F_{\mathrm{out}}(\hat{I}_{\mathrm{out}},\pi_{\mathrm{out}}^{(t-1)})\right|=\mathcal{O}(t^{-1})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>out</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>I</mi><mi>out</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>out</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>out</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>I</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>out</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>out</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left|F_{\mathrm{out}}(I_{\mathrm{out}}^{(t)},\pi_{\mathrm{out}}^{(t)})-F_{\mathrm{out}}(\hat{I}_{\mathrm{out}},\pi_{\mathrm{out}}^{(t-1)})\right|=\mathcal{O}(t^{-1}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(17)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS4.p1.7" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS4.p1.7.1" class="ltx_text">With Assumption <a href="#Thmassumption4" title="Assumption 4. ‣ 5.3 Gradient-Aligned Implicit Updates ‣ 5 Theoretical Analysis ‣ Graph-based Target Back-Propagation for Context Adaptation in Multi-LLM Agentic Systems" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>, with <math id="A1.SS4.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{I}_{\mathrm{out}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>I</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>out</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{I}_{\mathrm{out}}</annotation></semantics></math> we have</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex32" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex32.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y^{*}=M_{\mathrm{out}}\left(x,\hat{O}_{1},\dots,\hat{O}_{K};\pi_{\mathrm{out}}^{(t-1)}\right)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>out</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>O</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>O</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>K</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>out</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y^{*}=M_{\mathrm{out}}\left(x,\hat{O}_{1},\dots,\hat{O}_{K};\pi_{\mathrm{out}}^{(t-1)}\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS4.p1.8" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS4.p1.8.1" class="ltx_text">which results in</span></p>
<table id="A1.E18" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{\mathrm{out}}(\hat{I}_{\mathrm{out}},\pi_{\mathrm{out}}^{(t-1)})=F(\Pi_{\Phi}^{*})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>out</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>I</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>out</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>out</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{\mathrm{out}}(\hat{I}_{\mathrm{out}},\pi_{\mathrm{out}}^{(t-1)})=F(\Pi_{\Phi}^{*}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(18)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS4.p1.9" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS4.p1.9.1" class="ltx_text">Since</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex33" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex33.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{\mathrm{out}}(I_{\mathrm{out}}^{(t)},\pi_{\mathrm{out}}^{(t)})=F(\Pi_{\Phi}^{(t)})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>out</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>I</mi><mi>out</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>out</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{\mathrm{out}}(I_{\mathrm{out}}^{(t)},\pi_{\mathrm{out}}^{(t)})=F(\Pi_{\Phi}^{(t)}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS4.p1.10" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS4.p1.10.1" class="ltx_text">applying Eq. <a href="#A1.E18" title="In Proof. ‣ A.4 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix A Appendix of Theoretical Analysis ‣ Graph-based Target Back-Propagation for Context Adaptation in Multi-LLM Agentic Systems" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">18</span></a>, Eq. <a href="#A1.E17" title="In Proof. ‣ A.4 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix A Appendix of Theoretical Analysis ‣ Graph-based Target Back-Propagation for Context Adaptation in Multi-LLM Agentic Systems" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">17</span></a> becomes</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex34" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex34.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|F(\Pi_{\Phi}^{(t)})-F(\Pi_{\Phi}^{*})|=\mathcal{O}(t^{-1})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|F(\Pi_{\Phi}^{(t)})-F(\Pi_{\Phi}^{*})|=\mathcal{O}(t^{-1}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS4.p1.11" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS4.p1.11.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Appendix of Experiment</h2>

<div id="A2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">This section expands on the methodology and results introduced in Section <a href="#S6" title="6 Experiments ‣ Graph-based Target Back-Propagation for Context Adaptation in Multi-LLM Agentic Systems" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>, providing group-level breakdowns across demographic categories for the SubPOP dataset <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib29" title="" class="ltx_ref">Suh et al. (2025)</a></cite>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Table <a href="#A2.T4" title="Table 4 ‣ Appendix B Appendix of Experiment ‣ Graph-based Target Back-Propagation for Context Adaptation in Multi-LLM Agentic Systems" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a> compares our proposed algorithm against the self-reported performance metrics in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib29" title="" class="ltx_ref">Suh et al. (2025)</a></cite> and several baseline approaches.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Few-shot prompting</span>: We consider a conditioning prompt that includes group information along with the group’s response distribution over training questions, followed by the test question as the instruction prompt. In our experiments, we use 5 examples as the few-shot baseline.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Fine-tuned model</span>: We report benchmark metrics from <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib29" title="" class="ltx_ref">Suh et al. (2025)</a></cite>, where the authors fine-tuned several LLMs of varying parameter counts using the training data.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">GEPA</span>: We leverage GEPA <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib11" title="" class="ltx_ref">Agrawal et al. (2025)</a></cite> as a prompt training optimizer.
Example prompts trained using GEPA is provided in Appendix.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">GTBP</span>: Example prompts trained using GTBP are provided in Appendix.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p7.1" class="ltx_p">Our proposed approach (GTBP) achieves a lower average Wasserstein Distance (WD) than GEPA across demographic groups, demonstrating consistent improvements in bias mitigation without task-specific fine-tuning. Furthermore, when compared against fine-tuned models of similar parameter counts, specifically Llama-2-13B and Mistral-7B-v0.1, our approach still attains competitive or superior performance, highlighting its effectiveness as a model weight training alternative.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p8.1" class="ltx_p">However, our method does not outperform fine-tuned Llama-3-70B on average WD. We attribute this gap to two complementary factors: (1) the inherent representational capacity of larger models, which may enable more nuanced demographic inference by default, and (2) the benefit of supervised fine-tuning, which directly optimizes the model toward the target distribution. These results suggest that scaling model size or incorporating fine-tuning remain important considerations for future work.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A2.T4" class="ltx_table">
<div id="A2.T4.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_center ltx_transformed_outer" style="width:737.0pt;height:300.8pt;vertical-align:-147.9pt;"><span class="ltx_transformed_inner" style="transform:translate(0.0pt,0.0pt) scale(1,1) ;">
<p id="A2.T4.2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.T4.2.1.1" class="ltx_text">
<span id="A2.T4.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_tabular ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<span class="ltx_thead">
<span id="A2.T4.2.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_tr">
<span id="A2.T4.2.1.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_rowspan ltx_rowspan_2" style="padding-left:4.0pt;padding-right:4.0pt;"><span id="A2.T4.2.1.1.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text">Attribute</span></span>
<span id="A2.T4.2.1.1.1.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_rowspan ltx_rowspan_2" style="padding-left:4.0pt;padding-right:4.0pt;"><span id="A2.T4.2.1.1.1.1.2.1" class="ltx_text">Group</span></span>
<span id="A2.T4.2.1.1.1.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_rowspan ltx_rowspan_2" style="padding-left:4.0pt;padding-right:4.0pt;"><span id="A2.T4.2.1.1.1.1.3.1" class="ltx_text">Human Baseline</span></span>
<span id="A2.T4.2.1.1.1.1.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_colspan ltx_colspan_2" style="padding-left:4.0pt;padding-right:4.0pt;">Llama-2-7B</span>
<span id="A2.T4.2.1.1.1.1.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_colspan ltx_colspan_2" style="padding-left:4.0pt;padding-right:4.0pt;">Llama-2-13B</span>
<span id="A2.T4.2.1.1.1.1.6" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_colspan ltx_colspan_2" style="padding-left:4.0pt;padding-right:4.0pt;">Mistral-7B-v0.1</span>
<span id="A2.T4.2.1.1.1.1.7" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_colspan ltx_colspan_3" style="padding-left:4.0pt;padding-right:4.0pt;">GPT-4.1-mini</span>
<span id="A2.T4.2.1.1.1.1.8" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_colspan ltx_colspan_2" style="padding-left:4.0pt;padding-right:4.0pt;">Llama-3-70B</span></span>
